er\":\"Music: 8 hours (buds) \\/ 32 hours (case); Quick charge: 10 minutes = 3 hours playback.\"}]','[{\"accessed\":\"2026-11-23\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-01-27 18:15:00','2026-01-27 18:15:00'),(944,4,4,'OnePlus Nord Buds 3 Pro','oneplus-nord-buds-3-pro',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.00,NULL,0,'Rs 5,999 last listed price in Nepal','2024-10-07','discontinued',NULL,0,0,'<p>The OnePlus Nord Buds 3 Pro is no longer stocked in Nepal. Its last listed price was <strong>Rs 5,999</strong>. It launched in Nepal on 7 October 2024. We keep the full specs here for reference and for anyone checking a second-hand unit.</p>\n<p>Noise cancellation: Yes (Up to 49dB). Drivers: 12.4 mm dynamic drivers. Battery: Music: 12 hours (buds) / 44 hours (case), With ANC off, 50% volume, AAC; 1 hours (buds) / 1.33 hours (case), Quick charge: 10 minutes = 4 hours playback. Connectivity: Bluetooth 5.4, multipoint, Codecs: AAC, SBC. Water resistance: Earbuds: IP55 dust and splash resistance.</p>\n<p>Buying new instead? A current OnePlus alternative is the <a href=\"/products/oneplus-nord-buds-4\">OnePlus Nord Buds 4</a> (Rs 4,999).</p>','[{\"question\":\"Is the OnePlus Nord Buds 3 Pro still available in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"No, it is no longer stocked. Its last listed price was Rs 5,999.\"},{\"question\":\"When did the OnePlus Nord Buds 3 Pro launch in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"It launched in Nepal on 7 October 2024.\"},{\"question\":\"What is the OnePlus Nord Buds 3 Pro battery like?\",\"answer\":\"Music: 12 hours (buds) \\/ 44 hours (case), With ANC off, 50% volume, AAC; 1 hours (buds) \\/ 1.33 hours (case), Quick charge: 10 minutes = 4 hours playback.\"}]','[{\"accessed\":\"2026-11-23\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2024-10-06 18:15:00','2024-10-06 18:15:00'),(945,41,3,'Acer Swift Edge 14 AI SFE14-51T-960E 2025 (Intel Core Ultra 9 288V)','acer-swift-edge-14-ai-sfe14-51t-960e-2025-intel-core-ultra-9-288v',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,360000.00,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-01-01','available',NULL,0,0,'<p>The Acer Swift Edge 14 AI SFE14-51T-960E 2025 (Intel Core Ultra 9 288V) costs <strong>Rs 3,60,000</strong> in Nepal for the 32GB/1TB model. It launched in Nepal in 2026. This is high-end territory, aimed at heavy gaming, 3D work or video editing.</p>\n<p>It runs on the Intel Core Ultra 9 288V (TSMC N3B), 8 cores / 8 threads. Screen: 14 inches, OLED, WQXGA+ (2880 x 1800 pixels), 120Hz. 32GB of memory gives plenty of headroom for editing and development. At 0.99 kg, it is easy to carry every day. Battery: Li-Ion 65 Wh; 100W adapter.</p>\n<p>Around the same budget, also look at the <a href=\"/products/lenovo-yoga-9-14ill10-2025-core-ultra-7-258v\">Lenovo Yoga 9 Gen 5 14ILL10 2025 (Intel Core Ultra 7 258V)</a> (Rs 3,69,999) and the <a href=\"/products/lenovo-legion-7i-16iax10-2025-intel-core-ultra-9-275hx-rtx-5060\">Lenovo Legion 7i 16IAX10 2025 (Intel Core Ultra 9 275HX)</a> (Rs 3,49,999). You can <a href=\"/compare?category=laptop&g1=acer-swift-edge-14-ai-sfe14-51t-960e-2025-intel-core-ultra-9-288v&g2=lenovo-yoga-9-14ill10-2025-core-ultra-7-258v\">compare the Acer Swift Edge 14 AI SFE14-51T-960E 2025 (Intel Core Ultra 9 288V) with the Lenovo Yoga 9 Gen 5 14ILL10 2025 (Intel Core Ultra 7 258V)</a> side by side.</p>','[{\"question\":\"What is the Acer Swift Edge 14 AI SFE14-51T-960E 2025 (Intel Core Ultra 9 288V) price in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"The Acer Swift Edge 14 AI SFE14-51T-960E 2025 (Intel Core Ultra 9 288V) costs Rs 3,60,000 in Nepal.\"},{\"question\":\"When did the Acer Swift Edge 14 AI SFE14-51T-960E 2025 (Intel Core Ultra 9 288V) launch in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"It launched in Nepal in 2026.\"},{\"question\":\"Which processor does the Acer Swift Edge 14 AI SFE14-51T-960E 2025 (Intel Core Ultra 9 288V) use?\",\"answer\":\"It uses the Intel Core Ultra 9 288V (TSMC N3B), 8 cores \\/ 8 threads.\"}]','[{\"accessed\":\"2026-11-23\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2025-12-31 18:15:00','2025-12-31 18:15:00'),(946,3,2,'Redmi 15 4G','redmi-15-4g',NULL,'gadgets/2026/redmi-15-4g.webp',NULL,NULL,27999.00,NULL,0,NULL,'2025-09-01','available',NULL,0,0,'<p>The Redmi 15 4G is a big phone with a bigger battery: 6.9 inches, 144Hz and 7,000mAh for under Rs 28,000. Drivers, shopkeepers and people who watch a lot of video get two days from it without trying.</p>\n<p>The Snapdragon 685 is an older 4G chip, smooth for apps and limited for games. Make sure that your thumb can reach across the screen. For 5G and a newer chip, the Redmi 17 5G costs about Rs 6,000 more.</p>','[{\"question\":\"What is the Redmi 15 4G price in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"The Redmi 15 4G starts at Rs 27,999 in Nepal. All variants: Rs 27,999 for 6GB\\/128GB; Rs 29,999 for 8GB\\/256GB.\"},{\"question\":\"When did the Redmi 15 4G launch in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"It launched in Nepal on 1 September 2025.\"},{\"question\":\"Which processor does the Redmi 15 4G use?\",\"answer\":\"It uses the Qualcomm Snapdragon 685 (6nm).\"},{\"question\":\"What is the Redmi 15 4G battery like?\",\"answer\":\"Si-Ca 7000 mAh, non-removable; 33W Fast Charging.\"}]','[{\"accessed\":\"2026-11-23\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2025-08-31 18:15:00','2025-08-31 18:15:00'),(947,70,2,'Infinix GT 30 Pro','infinixgt-30-pro',NULL,'gadgets/2026/infinixgt-30-pro.webp',NULL,NULL,65999.00,NULL,0,NULL,'2025-06-24','available',NULL,0,0,'<p>The Infinix GT 30 Pro costs <strong>Rs 65,999</strong> in Nepal for the 8GB/256GB model. The 12GB/256GB version costs Rs 69,999. It launched in Nepal on 24 June 2025. At this price you should expect a bright AMOLED panel, a dependable main camera and long software support.</p>\n<p>It has a 6.78 Inches AMOLED, 144Hz, 700 nits (typ), 1600 nits (HBM), 4500 nits (HDR) screen and runs on the Mediatek Dimensity 8350 Ultimate (4nm). The 45W Fast Charging battery may need a top-up on heavy days. Charging: 30W Wireless Charging, 4.5W Reverse Wireless Charging. Cameras: Primary: 108MP, f/1.9, PDAF, 1/1.33” ISOCELL sensor + Ultrawide: 8MP, f/2.2, 111° FOV, 1/4.0\" sensor. It is rated IP64 for dust and water. Software support: 2 years of OS udpates; 3 years of security updates.</p>\n<p>Around the same budget, also look at the <a href=\"/products/tecno-camon-slim\">Tecno Camon Slim</a> (Rs 65,999) and the <a href=\"/products/realme-p3-ultra\">Realme P3 Ultra</a> (Rs 65,999). You can <a href=\"/compare?category=mobile&g1=infinixgt-30-pro&g2=tecno-camon-slim\">compare the Infinix GT 30 Pro with the Tecno Camon Slim</a> side by side.</p>','[{\"question\":\"What is the Infinix GT 30 Pro price in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"The Infinix GT 30 Pro starts at Rs 65,999 in Nepal. All variants: Rs 65,999 for 8GB\\/256GB; Rs 69,999 for 12GB\\/256GB.\"},{\"question\":\"When did the Infinix GT 30 Pro launch in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"It launched in Nepal on 24 June 2025.\"},{\"question\":\"Which processor does the Infinix GT 30 Pro use?\",\"answer\":\"It uses the Mediatek Dimensity 8350 Ultimate (4nm).\"},{\"question\":\"What is the Infinix GT 30 Pro battery like?\",\"answer\":\"45W Fast Charging; 30W Wireless Charging, 4.5W Reverse Wireless Charging.\"}]','[{\"accessed\":\"2026-11-23\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2025-06-23 18:15:00','2025-06-23 18:15:00'),(948,38,2,'Honor X7e Plus','honor-x7e-plus',NULL,'gadgets/2026/honor-x7e-plus.webp',NULL,NULL,44999.00,NULL,1,NULL,'2026-07-28','upcoming',NULL,0,0,'<p>The Honor X7e Plus has not launched in Nepal yet. Our expected price is <strong>Rs 44,999</strong>, an estimate until the official launch.</p>\n<p>It has a 6.87 inches TFT LCD, 120Hz, 1020 nits (peak), 860 nits (HBM) screen and runs on the Qualcomm Snapdragon 685 (6nm). The Si/C Li-Po 8100 mAh, non-removable battery is a real strength; most people will get a day and a half or more. Charging: 45W HONOR SuperCharge, 7.5W Reverse Charging. Cameras: Primary: 108MP f/1.8, AF + Auxiliary lens. It is rated IP68 / IP69K for dust and water. It is a 4G phone, which works fine on NTC and Ncell today but will not use 5G.</p>','[{\"question\":\"When will the Honor X7e Plus launch in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"It has not launched in Nepal yet. The expected price is around Rs 44,999.\"},{\"question\":\"Which processor does the Honor X7e Plus use?\",\"answer\":\"It uses the Qualcomm Snapdragon 685 (6nm).\"},{\"question\":\"What is the Honor X7e Plus battery like?\",\"answer\":\"Si\\/C Li-Po 8100 mAh, non-removable; 45W HONOR SuperCharge; 7.5W Reverse Charging.\"}]','[{\"accessed\":\"2026-11-23\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,4,'2026-07-27 18:15:00','2026-07-27 18:15:00'),(949,49,2,'Blackview Wave 7C','blackview-wave-7c',NULL,'gadgets/2026/blackview-wave-7c.webp',NULL,NULL,16999.00,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-19','available',NULL,0,0,'<p>The Blackview Wave 7C costs <strong>Rs 16,999</strong> in Nepal for the 4GB/64GB model. The 4GB/128GB version costs Rs 18,999. It launched in Nepal on 19 July 2026. At this price the job is simple: calls, messaging, social apps and a battery that lasts the day.</p>\n<p>It has a 6.56 inches IPS LCD, 60Hz, 430 (typ) screen and runs on the Unisoc Tiger T310 (12 nm). Its Li-Po 5000 mAh, non-removable battery should last a full day for most people. Charging: 10W charging. Cameras: Primary: 32MP, f/2.0, AF, 1/3.0” sensor. It is rated IP54 for dust and water. It is a 4G phone, which works fine on NTC and Ncell today but will not use 5G.</p>\n<p>Around the same budget, also look at the <a href=\"/products/infinix-hot-60i-4g\">Infinix Hot 60i 4G</a> (Rs 16,999) and the <a href=\"/products/realme-note-70\">Realme Note 70</a> (Rs 16,999). You can <a href=\"/compare?category=mobile&g1=blackview-wave-7c&g2=infinix-hot-60i-4g\">compare the Blackview Wave 7C with the Infinix Hot 60i 4G</a> side by side.</p>','[{\"question\":\"What is the Blackview Wave 7C price in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"The Blackview Wave 7C starts at Rs 16,999 in Nepal. All variants: Rs 16,999 for 4GB\\/64GB; Rs 18,999 for 4GB\\/128GB.\"},{\"question\":\"When did the Blackview Wave 7C launch in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"It launched in Nepal on 19 July 2026.\"},{\"question\":\"Which processor does the Blackview Wave 7C use?\",\"answer\":\"It uses the Unisoc Tiger T310 (12 nm).\"},{\"question\":\"What is the Blackview Wave 7C battery like?\",\"answer\":\"Li-Po 5000 mAh, non-removable; 10W charging.\"}]','[{\"accessed\":\"2026-11-23\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-07-18 18:15:00','2026-07-18 18:15:00'),(950,2,2,'iPhone 16e','iphone-16e',NULL,'gadgets/2026/iphone-16e.webp',NULL,NULL,0.00,NULL,0,'Rs 1,05,999 last listed price in Nepal','2025-02-21','discontinued',NULL,0,0,'<p>The iPhone 16e is no longer stocked in Nepal. Its last listed price was <strong>Rs 1,05,999</strong>. It launched in Nepal on 21 February 2025. We keep the full specs here for reference and for anyone checking a second-hand unit.</p>\n<p>It has a 6.1 inches Super Retina XDR OLED, 60Hz, 800 nits (HBM), 1200 nits (HDR) screen and runs on the Apple A18 (3 nm). The Li-Ion 4005 mAh, non-removable battery may need a top-up on heavy days. Charging: Wired, 50% in 30 min, 7.5W Wireless Charging. Cameras: 48MP, f/1.6, 26 mm, OIS, PDAF, 1/2.55” CMOS sensor. It is rated IP68 for dust and water. Software support: At least 5 years.</p>\n<p>Buying new instead? A current Apple alternative is the <a href=\"/products/apple-iphone-15\">iPhone 15</a> (Rs 1,27,499).</p>','[{\"question\":\"Is the iPhone 16e still available in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"No, it is no longer stocked. Its last listed price was Rs 1,05,999.\"},{\"question\":\"When did the iPhone 16e launch in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"It launched in Nepal on 21 February 2025.\"},{\"question\":\"Which processor does the iPhone 16e use?\",\"answer\":\"It uses the Apple A18 (3 nm).\"},{\"question\":\"What is the iPhone 16e battery like?\",\"answer\":\"Li-Ion 4005 mAh, non-removable; Wired, 50% in 30 min; 7.5W Wireless Charging.\"}]','[{\"accessed\":\"2026-11-23\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2025-02-20 18:15:00','2025-02-20 18:15:00'),(951,47,2,'Motorola Moto G05','moto-g05',NULL,'gadgets/2026/moto-g05.webp',NULL,NULL,0.00,NULL,0,'Rs 14,499 last listed price in Nepal','2025-04-17','discontinued',NULL,0,0,'<p>The Motorola Moto G05 is no longer stocked in Nepal. Its last listed price was <strong>Rs 14,499</strong>. It launched in Nepal on 17 April 2025. We keep the full specs here for reference and for anyone checking a second-hand unit.</p>\n<p>It has a 6.67 inches IPS LCD, 90Hz screen and runs on the Mediatek Helio G81 Extreme (12 nm). Its Li-ion 5200 mAh battery should last a full day for most people. Charging: 18W charging. Cameras: Primary: 50 MP, f/1.8, PDAF. It is a 4G phone, which works fine on NTC and Ncell today but will not use 5G.</p>\n<p>Buying new instead? A current Motorola alternative is the <a href=\"/products/motorola-moto-g35-5g\">Motorola Moto G35 5G</a> (Rs 30,699).</p>','[{\"question\":\"Is the Motorola Moto G05 still available in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"No, it is no longer stocked. Its last listed price was Rs 14,499.\"},{\"question\":\"When did the Motorola Moto G05 launch in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"It launched in Nepal on 17 April 2025.\"},{\"question\":\"Which processor does the Motorola Moto G05 use?\",\"answer\":\"It uses the Mediatek Helio G81 Extreme (12 nm).\"},{\"question\":\"What is the Motorola Moto G05 battery like?\",\"answer\":\"Li-ion 5200 mAh; 18W charging.\"}]','[{\"accessed\":\"2026-11-23\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2025-04-16 18:15:00','2025-04-16 18:15:00'),(952,71,2,'Ai+ Pulse','ai-plus-plus',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,14999.00,NULL,0,NULL,'2025-09-07','available',NULL,0,0,'<p>The Ai+ Pulse costs <strong>Rs 14,999</strong> in Nepal for the 4GB/64GB model. The 6GB/128GB version costs Rs 16,499. It launched in Nepal on 7 September 2025. At this price the job is simple: calls, messaging, social apps and a battery that lasts the day.</p>\n<p>It has a 6.745 inches TFT LCD, 90Hz screen and runs on the Unisoc T615 4G (12nm). Its Li-Po 5000 mAh, non-removable battery should last a full day for most people. Cameras: Primary: 50MP sensor. It is a 4G phone, which works fine on NTC and Ncell today but will not use 5G.</p>\n<p>Around the same budget, also look at the <a href=\"/products/infinix-smart-10\">Infinix Smart 10</a> (Rs 14,999) and the <a href=\"/products/blackview-wave-10c\">Blackview Wave 10C</a> (Rs 14,499). You can <a href=\"/compare?category=mobile&g1=ai-plus-plus&g2=infinix-smart-10\">compare the Ai+ Pulse with the Infinix Smart 10</a> side by side.</p>','[{\"question\":\"What is the Ai+ Pulse price in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"The Ai+ Pulse starts at Rs 14,999 in Nepal. All variants: Rs 14,999 for 4GB\\/64GB; Rs 16,499 for 6GB\\/128GB.\"},{\"question\":\"When did the Ai+ Pulse launch in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"It launched in Nepal on 7 September 2025.\"},{\"question\":\"Which processor does the Ai+ Pulse use?\",\"answer\":\"It uses the Unisoc T615 4G (12nm).\"},{\"question\":\"What is the Ai+ Pulse battery like?\",\"answer\":\"Li-Po 5000 mAh, non-removable.\"}]','[{\"accessed\":\"2026-11-23\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2025-09-06 18:15:00','2025-09-06 18:15:00'),(953,3,2,'POCO M8s','poco-m8s',NULL,'gadgets/2026/poco-m8s.webp',NULL,NULL,39999.00,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-05','available',NULL,0,0,'<p>POCO\'s M8s is for people who want a huge, smooth screen and a long day. The 6.9-inch 144Hz AMOLED and 7,000mAh battery make films and maps a pleasure at Rs 39,999.</p>\n<p>The Snapdragon 6s Gen 3 is modest for a brand known for speed, and the display\'s 850 nits is dimmer outdoors than rivals at this price. Choose 8GB. If you play games, an Infinix Note 50s is faster for less. If you stream on the road, the POCO makes sense.</p>','[{\"question\":\"What is the POCO M8s price in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"The POCO M8s starts at Rs 39,999 in Nepal. All variants: Rs 39,999 for 6GB\\/128GB; Rs 46,999 for 8GB\\/256GB.\"},{\"question\":\"When did the POCO M8s launch in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"It launched in Nepal on 5 July 2026.\"},{\"question\":\"Which processor does the POCO M8s use?\",\"answer\":\"It uses the Qualcomm Snapdragon 6s Gen 3 (6 nm).\"},{\"question\":\"What is the POCO M8s battery like?\",\"answer\":\"Si-C 7000 mAh, non-removable; 33W Charging; 18W Reverse Wired Charging.\"}]','[{\"accessed\":\"2026-11-23\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-07-04 18:15:00','2026-07-04 18:15:00'),(954,3,2,'POCO M8 Pro','poco-m8-pro',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,58999.00,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-05','available',NULL,0,0,'<p>The POCO M8 Pro costs <strong>Rs 58,999</strong> in Nepal for the 8GB/256GB model. It launched in Nepal on 5 July 2026. This is the sweet spot: enough for an AMOLED screen and fast charging without paying for flagship cameras.</p>\n<p>It has a 6.83 inches AMOLED, 120Hz, 1800 nits (HBM), 3200 nits (Peak) screen and runs on the Qualcomm Snapdragon 7s Gen 4 (4nm). Its Si-C 6500 mAh, non-removable battery should last a full day for most people. Charging: 100W HyperCharge, 22.5W Reverse Wired Charging. Cameras: Primary: 50MP, f/1.6, 24 mm, OIS, PDAF, 1/1.55\" Light Fusion 800 sensor + Ultrawide: 8MP, f/2.2, 15 mm, 120° FOV, 1/4.0\"OV08D sensor. It is rated IP66/IP68/IP69/IP69K for dust and water. Software support: 4 years of OS updates; 6 years of security updates.</p>\n<p>Around the same budget, also look at the <a href=\"/products/redmi-note-17-pro-5g\">Redmi Note 17 Pro 5G</a> (Rs 57,999) and the <a href=\"/products/poco-x7-pro\">Poco X7 Pro</a> (Rs 59,999). You can <a href=\"/compare?category=mobile&g1=poco-m8-pro&g2=redmi-note-17-pro-5g\">compare the POCO M8 Pro with the Redmi Note 17 Pro 5G</a> side by side.</p>','[{\"question\":\"What is the POCO M8 Pro price in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"The POCO M8 Pro costs Rs 58,999 in Nepal.\"},{\"question\":\"When did the POCO M8 Pro launch in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"It launched in Nepal on 5 July 2026.\"},{\"question\":\"Which processor does the POCO M8 Pro use?\",\"answer\":\"It uses the Qualcomm Snapdragon 7s Gen 4 (4nm).\"},{\"question\":\"What is the POCO M8 Pro battery like?\",\"answer\":\"Si-C 6500 mAh, non-removable; 100W HyperCharge; 22.5W Reverse Wired Charging.\"}]','[{\"accessed\":\"2026-11-23\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-07-04 18:15:00','2026-07-04 18:15:00'),(955,3,2,'Poco F8 Pro','poco-f8-pro',NULL,'gadgets/2026/poco-f8-pro.webp',NULL,NULL,104999.00,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-02-12','available',NULL,0,0,'<p>The Poco F8 Pro costs <strong>Rs 1,04,999</strong> in Nepal for the 12GB/512GB model. It launched in Nepal on 12 February 2026. That is flagship money, so the camera system, the chip and the build quality all need to justify it.</p>\n<p>It has a 6.83 inches AMOLED, 120Hz, 2000 nits (HBM), 3500 nits (Peak) screen and runs on the Qualcomm Snapdragon 8 Elite (3nm). Its Si-Ca 6500 mAh, non-removable battery should last a full day for most people. Charging: 100W HyperCharge. Cameras: Primary: 50MP, f/1.9, 24 mm, OIS, PDAF, 1/1.55\" Light Fusion 800 sensor + Telephoto: 50MP, f/2.2, 60 mm, 2.5x optical zoom, PDAF, 1/2.88\" OV50M sensor + Ultrawide: 8MP, f/2.2, 15 mm, 120° FOV, 1/4.0\"OV08D sensor. It is rated IP68 for dust and water. Software support: 4 years of OS updates; 6 years of security updates.</p>\n<p>Around the same budget, also look at the <a href=\"/products/vivo-v80\">vivo V80</a> (Rs 1,08,999) and the <a href=\"/products/nothing-phone-3\">Nothing Phone (3)</a> (Rs 1,09,999). You can <a href=\"/compare?category=mobile&g1=poco-f8-pro&g2=vivo-v80\">compare the Poco F8 Pro with the vivo V80</a> side by side.</p>','[{\"question\":\"What is the Poco F8 Pro price in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"The Poco F8 Pro costs Rs 1,04,999 in Nepal.\"},{\"question\":\"When did the Poco F8 Pro launch in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"It launched in Nepal on 12 February 2026.\"},{\"question\":\"Which processor does the Poco F8 Pro use?\",\"answer\":\"It uses the Qualcomm Snapdragon 8 Elite (3nm).\"},{\"question\":\"What is the Poco F8 Pro battery like?\",\"answer\":\"Si-Ca 6500 mAh, non-removable; 100W HyperCharge.\"}]','[{\"accessed\":\"2026-11-23\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-02-11 18:15:00','2026-02-11 18:15:00'),(956,3,2,'Poco X7 Pro','poco-x7-pro',NULL,'gadgets/2026/poco-x7-pro.webp',NULL,NULL,59999.00,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-02-12','available',NULL,0,0,'<p>A year on, the X7 Pro remains a quiet bargain. The Dimensity 8400 Ultra is only a little behind phones that cost twice as much, 12GB and 512GB come as standard, and 90W charging refills 6,000mAh in under an hour.</p>\n<p>It takes good photos with the main camera and forgettable ones with the ultra wide. The design is loud in yellow and calmer in other colours. With the F7 above it and cheaper Redmis below, its price has room to be negotiated, and under Rs 55,000 it is hard to resist. <a href=\"/reviews/poco-x7-pro-review-nepal\">Our review</a> goes further.</p>','[{\"question\":\"What is the Poco X7 Pro price in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"The Poco X7 Pro costs Rs 59,999 in Nepal.\"},{\"question\":\"When did the Poco X7 Pro launch in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"It launched in Nepal on 12 February 2026.\"},{\"question\":\"Which processor does the Poco X7 Pro use?\",\"answer\":\"It uses the Mediatek Dimensity 8400 Ultra (4nm).\"},{\"question\":\"What is the Poco X7 Pro battery like?\",\"answer\":\"Si-Ca 6000 mAh, non-removable; 90W HyperCharge.\"}]','[{\"accessed\":\"2026-11-23\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-02-11 18:15:00','2026-02-11 18:15:00'),(957,3,2,'Poco F7','poco-f7',NULL,'gadgets/2026/poco-f7.webp',NULL,NULL,69999.00,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-02-12','available',NULL,0,0,'<p>The POCO F7 is bought for one reason, speed, and turns out to be good at more than that. A Snapdragon 8s Gen 4 with 12GB of memory and 512GB of very fast storage runs any game sold today, and the 6,500mAh battery with 90W charging keeps up with it. IP68 protection is a welcome extra at this price.</p>\n<p>It gives up camera range: the main sensor is stabilised and reliable, while the ultra wide is ordinary and there is no zoom lens. HyperOS also needs an evening of tidying. If you play or multitask hard, few phones under Rs 1 lakh make more sense. <a href=\"/reviews/poco-f7-review-nepal\">Read our full view of it</a>.</p>','[{\"question\":\"What is the Poco F7 price in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"The Poco F7 costs Rs 69,999 in Nepal.\"},{\"question\":\"When did the Poco F7 launch in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"It launched in Nepal on 12 February 2026.\"},{\"question\":\"Which processor does the Poco F7 use?\",\"answer\":\"It uses the Qualcomm Snapdragon 8s Gen 4 (4nm).\"},{\"question\":\"What is the Poco F7 battery like?\",\"answer\":\"Si-Ca 6500 mAh, non-removable; 90W Fast Charging.\"}]','[{\"accessed\":\"2026-11-23\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,5,'2026-02-11 18:15:00','2026-11-24 07:52:54'),(958,47,2,'Motorola Moto G85 5G','moto-g85-5g',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.00,NULL,0,'Rs 34,499 last listed price in Nepal','2024-07-10','discontinued',NULL,0,0,'<p>The Motorola Moto G85 5G is no longer stocked in Nepal. Its last listed price was <strong>Rs 34,499</strong>. It launched in Nepal on 10 July 2024. We keep the full specs here for reference and for anyone checking a second-hand unit.</p>\n<p>It has a 6.67 inches P-OLED, 120Hz, 1600 nits (HDR) screen and runs on the Qualcomm Snapdragon 6s Gen 3 (6nm). Its Li-ion 5000 mAh, non-removable battery should last a full day for most people. Charging: 30W Fast Charging. Cameras: Primary: 50MP, f/1.8, OIS, PDAF 1/1.95” LYT-600 sensor + Ultrawide: 8MP, f/2.2, 118° FOV. It is rated IP52 for dust and water. Software support: 2 years of OS udpates; 4 years of security updates.</p>\n<p>Buying new instead? A current Motorola alternative is the <a href=\"/products/moto-g06-power\">Motorola Moto G06 Power</a> (Rs 31,999).</p>','[{\"question\":\"Is the Motorola Moto G85 5G still available in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"No, it is no longer stocked. Its last listed price was Rs 34,499.\"},{\"question\":\"When did the Motorola Moto G85 5G launch in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"It launched in Nepal on 10 July 2024.\"},{\"question\":\"Which processor does the Motorola Moto G85 5G use?\",\"answer\":\"It uses the Qualcomm Snapdragon 6s Gen 3 (6nm).\"},{\"question\":\"What is the Motorola Moto G85 5G battery like?\",\"answer\":\"Li-ion 5000 mAh, non-removable; 30W Fast Charging.\"}]','[{\"accessed\":