, 1/3.2” sensor. Software support: 7 years of OS updates; 7 years of security updates.</p>\n<p>Around the same budget, also look at the <a href=\"/products/iphone-17e\">iPhone 17e</a> (Rs 1,32,499) and the <a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-s26\">Samsung Galaxy S26</a> (Rs 1,39,999). You can <a href=\"/compare?category=mobile&g1=samsung-galaxy-z-flip7-fe&g2=iphone-17e\">compare the Samsung Galaxy Z Flip 7 FE with the iPhone 17e</a> side by side.</p>','[{\"question\":\"What is the Samsung Galaxy Z Flip 7 FE price in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"The Samsung Galaxy Z Flip 7 FE costs Rs 1,35,999 in Nepal.\"},{\"question\":\"Which processor does the Samsung Galaxy Z Flip 7 FE use?\",\"answer\":\"It uses the Samsung Exynos 2400 (4nm).\"},{\"question\":\"What is the Samsung Galaxy Z Flip 7 FE battery like?\",\"answer\":\"Li-Po 4000 mAh, non-removable; 25W Fast Charging; 15W Wireless Charging, 4.5W Reverse Wireless Charging.\"}]','[{\"accessed\":\"2026-11-23\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2025-07-09 18:15:00','2025-07-09 18:15:00'),(1022,73,2,'Google Pixel 10a','google-pixel-10a',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,86000.00,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-02-18','available',NULL,0,0,'<p>The Google Pixel 10a costs <strong>Rs 86,000</strong> in Nepal for the 8GB/128GB model. It was announced on 18 February 2026. At this price you should expect a bright AMOLED panel, a dependable main camera and long software support.</p>\n<p>It has a 6.3 inches OLED, 120Hz, 2000 nits (HBM), 3000 nits (HDR) screen and runs on the Google Tensor G4 (4nm). Its Li-Po 5100 mAh, non-removable battery should last a full day for most people. Charging: 30W charger, 10W wireless charging. Cameras: Primary: 48MP, f/1.7, 25 mm, OIS, PDAF, 1/2.0\" sensor + Ultrawide: 13MP, f/2.2, PDAF, 120° FOV, 1/3.1\" sensor. It is rated IP68 for dust and water. Software support: 7 years of OS updates; 7 years of security updates.</p>\n<p>Around the same budget, also look at the <a href=\"/products/honor-600\">Honor 600</a> (Rs 84,999) and the <a href=\"/products/infinix-gt-50-pro\">Infinix GT 50 Pro</a> (Rs 84,999). You can <a href=\"/compare?category=mobile&g1=google-pixel-10a&g2=honor-600\">compare the Google Pixel 10a with the Honor 600</a> side by side.</p>','[{\"question\":\"What is the Google Pixel 10a price in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"The Google Pixel 10a costs Rs 86,000 in Nepal.\"},{\"question\":\"Which processor does the Google Pixel 10a use?\",\"answer\":\"It uses the Google Tensor G4 (4nm).\"},{\"question\":\"What is the Google Pixel 10a battery like?\",\"answer\":\"Li-Po 5100 mAh, non-removable; 30W charger; 10W wireless charging.\"}]','[{\"accessed\":\"2026-11-23\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-02-17 18:15:00','2026-02-17 18:15:00'),(1023,38,2,'Honor X5d Plus','honor-x5d-plus',NULL,'gadgets/2026/honor-x5d-plus.webp',NULL,NULL,28999.00,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-08-07','available',NULL,0,0,'<p>The Honor X5d Plus costs <strong>Rs 28,999</strong> in Nepal for the 4GB/128GB model. It launched in Nepal on 7 August 2026. It sits in the busiest part of the market, where battery life and a smooth screen matter more than benchmark scores.</p>\n<p>It has a 6.74 inches TFT LCD, 90Hz screen and runs on the Mediatek Helio G81 (12nm). Its Li-Po 5260 mAh, non-removable battery should last a full day for most people. Charging: 15W charging. Cameras: Primary: 50 MP, f/1.8, PDAF + Auxiliary lens. It is a 4G phone, which works fine on NTC and Ncell today but will not use 5G.</p>\n<p>Around the same budget, also look at the <a href=\"/products/realme-c100i\">Realme C100i</a> (Rs 28,999) and the <a href=\"/products/zte-nubia-v80-max\">ZTE Nubia V80 Max</a> (Rs 29,499). You can <a href=\"/compare?category=mobile&g1=honor-x5d-plus&g2=realme-c100i\">compare the Honor X5d Plus with the Realme C100i</a> side by side.</p>','[{\"question\":\"What is the Honor X5d Plus price in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"The Honor X5d Plus costs Rs 28,999 in Nepal.\"},{\"question\":\"When did the Honor X5d Plus launch in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"It launched in Nepal on 7 August 2026.\"},{\"question\":\"Which processor does the Honor X5d Plus use?\",\"answer\":\"It uses the Mediatek Helio G81 (12nm).\"},{\"question\":\"What is the Honor X5d Plus battery like?\",\"answer\":\"Li-Po 5260 mAh, non-removable; 15W charging.\"}]','[{\"accessed\":\"2026-11-23\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-08-06 18:15:00','2026-08-06 18:15:00'),(1024,72,2,'ZTE Nubia V80 Max','zte-nubia-v80-max',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,29499.00,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-01-13','available',NULL,0,0,'<p>The ZTE Nubia V80 Max costs <strong>Rs 29,499</strong> in Nepal for the 8GB/128GB model. The 8GB/256GB version costs Rs 31,499. It launched in Nepal on 13 January 2026. It sits in the busiest part of the market, where battery life and a smooth screen matter more than benchmark scores.</p>\n<p>It has a 6.9 inches IPS LCD, 120Hz, 780 nits (HBM) screen and runs on the Unisoc T7250 (12nm). Its Li-ion 6000 mAh, non-removable battery should last a full day for most people. Charging: 22.5W Fast Charging. Cameras: Primary: 50MP, f/1.8 + Depth: 2MP + Auxiliary lens. It is rated IP64 for dust and water. It is a 4G phone, which works fine on NTC and Ncell today but will not use 5G.</p>\n<p>Around the same budget, also look at the <a href=\"/products/realme-c100i\">Realme C100i</a> (Rs 28,999) and the <a href=\"/products/honor-x6d\">Honor X6d</a> (Rs 29,999). You can <a href=\"/compare?category=mobile&g1=zte-nubia-v80-max&g2=realme-c100i\">compare the ZTE Nubia V80 Max with the Realme C100i</a> side by side.</p>','[{\"question\":\"What is the ZTE Nubia V80 Max price in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"The ZTE Nubia V80 Max starts at Rs 29,499 in Nepal. All variants: Rs 29,499 for 8GB\\/128GB; Rs 31,499 for 8GB\\/256GB.\"},{\"question\":\"When did the ZTE Nubia V80 Max launch in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"It launched in Nepal on 13 January 2026.\"},{\"question\":\"Which processor does the ZTE Nubia V80 Max use?\",\"answer\":\"It uses the Unisoc T7250 (12nm).\"},{\"question\":\"What is the ZTE Nubia V80 Max battery like?\",\"answer\":\"Li-ion 6000 mAh, non-removable; 22.5W Fast Charging.\"}]','[{\"accessed\":\"2026-11-23\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-01-12 18:15:00','2026-01-12 18:15:00'),(1025,38,2,'Honor X8c','honor-x8c',NULL,'gadgets/2026/honor-x8c.webp',NULL,NULL,0.00,NULL,0,'Rs 33,999 last listed price in Nepal','2024-02-28','discontinued',NULL,0,0,'<p>The Honor X8c is no longer stocked in Nepal. Its last listed price was <strong>Rs 33,999</strong>. It launched in Nepal on 28 February 2024. We keep the full specs here for reference and for anyone checking a second-hand unit.</p>\n<p>It has a 6.7 inches AMOLED, 120 Hz, 1200 nits (HBM), 2800 nits (HDR) screen and runs on the Qualcomm Snapdragon 685 4G (6nm). Its Li-Po 5000 mAh, non-removable battery should last a full day for most people. Charging: 35W Honor SuperCharge. Cameras: Primary: 108MP, f/1.8, 24 mm, OIS, PDAF, 1/1.67” CMOS BSI sensor + Ultrawide: 5MP, f/2.2. It is rated IP64 for dust and water. It is a 4G phone, which works fine on NTC and Ncell today but will not use 5G.</p>\n<p>Buying new instead? A current Honor alternative is the <a href=\"/products/honor-x7d\">Honor X7d</a> (Rs 33,999).</p>','[{\"question\":\"Is the Honor X8c still available in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"No, it is no longer stocked. Its last listed price was Rs 33,999.\"},{\"question\":\"When did the Honor X8c launch in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"It launched in Nepal on 28 February 2024.\"},{\"question\":\"Which processor does the Honor X8c use?\",\"answer\":\"It uses the Qualcomm Snapdragon 685 4G (6nm).\"},{\"question\":\"What is the Honor X8c battery like?\",\"answer\":\"Li-Po 5000 mAh, non-removable; 35W Honor SuperCharge.\"}]','[{\"accessed\":\"2026-11-23\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2024-02-27 18:15:00','2024-02-27 18:15:00');
