00,NULL,0,NULL,'2025-08-15','available',NULL,0,0,'<p>For a student with Rs 36,000, the Note 50s is close to ideal. A Dimensity 7300 Ultimate with fast memory and storage keeps games steady, the 144Hz AMOLED looks far more expensive, and the stabilised 64MP camera takes usable photos after sunset.</p>\n<p>The 5,200mAh battery is average beside today\'s giants, and Infinix has fewer service points and shorter updates than Samsung or Xiaomi. Check which variant is in the box, since 4G and 5G versions exist under similar names. If service is available near you, nothing else at the price is as complete.</p>','[{\"question\":\"What is the Infinix Note 50s price in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"The Infinix Note 50s costs Rs 35,999 in Nepal.\"},{\"question\":\"When did the Infinix Note 50s launch in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"It launched in Nepal on 15 August 2025.\"},{\"question\":\"Which processor does the Infinix Note 50s use?\",\"answer\":\"It uses the Mediatek Dimensity 7300 Ultimate (4nm).\"},{\"question\":\"What is the Infinix Note 50s battery like?\",\"answer\":\"Li-Po 5200 mAh, non-removable; 45W Fast Charging.\"}]','[{\"accessed\":\"2026-11-23\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2025-08-14 18:15:00','2025-08-14 18:15:00'),(1378,70,2,'Infinix Hot 60 Pro','infinix-hot-60-pro',NULL,'gadgets/2026/infinix-hot-60-pro.webp',NULL,NULL,0.00,NULL,0,'Rs 24,999 last listed price in Nepal','2025-02-26','discontinued',NULL,0,0,'<p>The Infinix Hot 60 Pro is no longer stocked in Nepal. Its last listed price was <strong>Rs 24,999</strong>. It was announced on 26 February 2025. We keep the full specs here for reference and for anyone checking a second-hand unit.</p>\n<p>It has a 6.78 inches AMOLED, 144Hz, 700 nits (typ), 1600 nits (HBM), 4500 nits (HDR) screen and runs on the Mediatek Helio G200 (6nm). Its Li-Po 5160 mAh, non-removable battery should last a full day for most people. Charging: 45W Fast Charging. Cameras: Primary: 50MP, f/1.6, 27 mm, PDAF, 1/2.8\" CMOS sensor + Auxiliary lens. It is rated IP64 for dust and water. Software support: 3 years of OS updates; 5 years of security updates. It is a 4G phone, which works fine on NTC and Ncell today but will not use 5G.</p>\n<p>Buying new instead? A current Infinix alternative is the <a href=\"/products/infinix-hot-50-pro-plus\">Infinix Hot 50 Pro Plus</a> (Rs 25,999).</p>','[{\"question\":\"Is the Infinix Hot 60 Pro still available in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"No, it is no longer stocked. Its last listed price was Rs 24,999.\"},{\"question\":\"Which processor does the Infinix Hot 60 Pro use?\",\"answer\":\"It uses the Mediatek Helio G200 (6nm).\"},{\"question\":\"What is the Infinix Hot 60 Pro battery like?\",\"answer\":\"Li-Po 5160 mAh, non-removable; 45W Fast Charging.\"}]','[{\"accessed\":\"2026-11-23\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2025-02-25 18:15:00','2025-02-25 18:15:00'),(1379,36,2,'CMF Phone 1','cmf-phone-1',NULL,'gadgets/2026/cmf-phone-1.webp',NULL,NULL,0.00,NULL,0,'Rs 31,699 last listed price in Nepal','2024-07-08','discontinued',NULL,0,0,'<p>The CMF Phone 1 is no longer stocked in Nepal. Its last listed price was <strong>Rs 31,699</strong>. It launched in Nepal on 8 July 2024. We keep the full specs here for reference and for anyone checking a second-hand unit.</p>\n<p>It has a 6.67 inches Super AMOLED, 120Hz, 500 nits (typ), 2000 nits (HDR) screen and runs on the Mediatek Dimensity 7300 (4nm). Its Li-Po 5000 mAh, non-removable battery should last a full day for most people. Charging: 33W Fast Charging. Cameras: Primary: 50MP, f/1.8, 26 mm, OIS, PDAF, 1/1.9” IMX882 sensor + Depth: 2MP, f/2.4. It is rated IP52 for dust and water. Software support: 2 years of OS udpates; 3 years of security updates.</p>\n<p>Buying new instead? A current Nothing alternative is the <a href=\"/products/nothing-phone-3a-lite\">Nothing Phone 3a Lite</a> (Rs 54,999).</p>','[{\"question\":\"Is the CMF Phone 1 still available in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"No, it is no longer stocked. Its last listed price was Rs 31,699.\"},{\"question\":\"When d